# text = ' Liza-Lu then went to bed , and Tess , locking them all in , started on her way up the dark and crooked lane or street not made for hasty progress ; a street laid out before inches of land had value , and when one-handed clocks sufficiently subdivided the day Rolliver's inn , the single alehouse at this end of the long and broken village , could only boast of an off-licence ; hence , as nobody could legally drink on the premises , the amount of overt accommodation for consumers was strictly limited to a little board about six inches wide and two yards long , fixed to the garden palings by pieces of wire , so as to form a ledge .
