# text = But Tess's pride made the part of poor relation one of particular distaste to her she murmured said his wife , turning to where he sat in the background murmured he His reasons for staying away were worse to Tess than her own objections to going she said mournfully observed her father sententiously asked Joan Rising early next day she walked to the hill-town called Shaston , and there took advantage of a van which twice in the week ran from Shaston eastward to Chaseborough , passing near Trantridge , the parish in which the vague and mysterious Mrs d'Urberville had her residence .
