# text = With the impulse of a soul who could feel for kindred sufferers as much as for herself , Tess's first thought was to put the still living birds out of their torture , and to this end with her own hands she broke the necks of as many as she could find , leaving them to lie where she had found them till the game-keepers should come -- as they probably would come -- to look for them a second time she exclaimed , her tears running down as she killed the birds tenderly She was ashamed of herself for her gloom of the night , based on nothing more tangible than a sense of condemnation under an arbitrary law of society which had no foundation in Nature
