# text = After this season of congealed dampness came a spell of dry frost , when strange birds from behind the North Pole began to arrive silently on the upland of Flintcomb-Ash ; gaunt spectral creatures with tragical eyes -- eyes which had witnessed scenes of cataclysmal horror in inaccessible polar regions of a magnitude such as no human being had ever conceived , in curdling temperatures that no man could endure ; which had beheld the crash of icebergs and the slide of snow-hills by the shooting light of the Aurora ; been half blinded by the whirl of colossal storms and terraqueous distortions ; and retained the expression of feature that such scenes had engendered .
