# text = A year had now elapsed since her sad marriage , but she had preserved sufficient draperies from the wreck of her then full wardrobe to clothe her very charmingly as a simple country girl with no pretensions to recent fashion ; a soft gray woollen gown , with white crape quilling against the pink skin of her face and neck , and a black velvet jacket and hat said Izz Huett , regarding Tess as she stood on the threshold between the steely starlight without and the yellow candlelight within .
