# text = Hard by , the aisle of the church called the d'Urberville Aisle looked on imperturbably said Tess's mother , as she returned from a reconnoitre of the church and graveyard Tess listlessly lent a hand , and in a quarter of an hour the old four-post bedstead was dissociated from the heap of goods , and erected under the south wall of the church , the part of the building known as the d'Urberville Aisle , beneath which the huge vaults lay .
